    {"en", "show\n  Not available in this build: the connection runs the SFTP\n  subsystem, so remote shell commands cannot be shown.", "show\n  Not available in this build: the connection runs the SFTP\n  subsystem, so remote shell commands cannot be shown."},
    {"en", "stat <file>\n  Prints the listing line of a remote path, as ls -l shows\n  it. The key/value breakdown of attr stays available there.", "stat <file>\n  Prints the listing line of a remote path, as ls -l shows\n  it. The key/value breakdown of attr stays available there."},
    {"en", "supported: echo, batch, confirm, resume, transfer, include, exclude, failonnomatch, synchdelete, reconnecttime, editor, editmaxsize, preset", "supported: echo, batch, confirm, resume, transfer, include, exclude, failonnomatch, synchdelete, reconnecttime, editor, editmaxsize, preset"},
    {"en", "symlink <target> <link>\n  Same as 'ln'.", "symlink <target> <link>\n  Same as 'ln'."},
    {"en", "synchronize local|remote|both [ <localdir> [ <remotedir> ] ]\n  [ -delete ] [-nodelete] [-mirror] [-preview]\n  [-criteria=time|size|checksum|either|both|none] [-filemask=<mask>]\n  [-transfer=binary|ascii|automatic] [-nonrecursive]\n  The criteria say what counts as a change: 'time' (the\n  default) copies a file the source has newer, 'size' one of\n  a different size, 'checksum' one whose contents differ and\n  'none' every file. 'either' and its synonym 'both' compare\n  the time and the size, and the three comparisons may also\n  be listed, as in -criteria=time,checksum. In the 'both'\n  direction the record of the previous synchronization\n  decides, so 'checksum' and 'none' are refused there.", "synchronize local|remote|both [ <localdir> [ <remotedir> ] ]\n  [ -delete ] [-nodelete] [-mirror] [-preview]\n  [-criteria=time|size|checksum|either|both|none] [-filemask=<mask>]\n  [-transfer=binary|ascii|automatic] [-nonrecursive]\n  The criteria say what counts as a change: 'time' (the\n  default) copies a file the source has newer, 'size' one of\n  a different size, 'checksum' one whose contents differ and\n  'none' every file. 'either' and its synonym 'both' compare\n  the time and the size, and the three comparisons may also\n  be listed, as in -criteria=time,checksum. In the 'both'\n  direction the record of the previous synchronization\n  decides, so 'checksum' and 'none' are refused there."},
    {"en", "terminal\n  Opens an interactive shell terminal on the server.", "terminal\n  Opens an interactive shell terminal on the server."},
